; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Starry Night Sky
; CATEGORY: Generative Art & Colour
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     random, DOT, stars, moon, night
; SUMMARY:  Fills a dark sky with random stars, a few bright twinkles and a crescent moon.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Sprinkles hundreds of tiny stars of different brightness over a
;   deep blue sky. A few big stars get four little rays. Two dots,
;   one bright and one the color of the sky, make a crescent moon.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Every run makes a new sky.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * DOT and SETPENSIZE for points of any size
;   * using one random number for all three colors to get greys
;   * painting over something with the background color
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make a few stars slightly yellow or blue.
;   * Move the dark dot to change the shape of the moon.
;   * Add a dark hill along the bottom with a thick line.
; ============================================================

; TINY.STAR puts a small star anywhere. Using the same number for
; red, green and blue gives a grey, from dim to bright white.
to tiny.star
  localmake "light (random 90 255)
  setpencolor (list :light :light :light)
  setpensize (random 1 3)
  dot list (random -400 400) (random -300 300)
end

; TWINKLE draws a bright star with four rays at (x, y).
to twinkle :x :y
  setpencolor [255 255 220]
  setpensize 5
  dot list :x :y
  setpensize 1
  repeat 4 [
    penup setxy :x :y pendown
    setheading 90 * repcount
    forward 12
  ]
end

; MOON makes a crescent: a bright disk, then a disk of sky color
; slightly to one side that covers most of it.
to moon :x :y
  setpencolor [250 240 200]
  setpensize 110
  dot list :x :y
  setpencolor background
  setpensize 100
  dot list :x - 30 :y + 15
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [10 15 45]
repeat 500 [tiny.star]
repeat 12 [twinkle (random -380 380) (random -280 280)]
moon 250 170
